 "poem": "The current world with many\nHallows and hinds, many\nBishops and choirs of young women\nIn troupes and handsome dress\nMust dance and twine amain at every\nStep which the fountains tread. - O heaven!\nWe see your servants ne'er to depart!\nThere was not a sound in Heaven to\nFear their work while they performed\nFor us on her altar.\nAnd there were none but angels among\nWhose cloaks or folds never",
